      "text": "**Adding Angular Support**\n\nI\u0027m currently fleshing out the implications of adding Angular to the comparison matrix. My focus is on how the Gingee SPA architecture fares against Angular\u0027s strengths and weaknesses. I\u0027m aiming to showcase its adaptability in handling a completely different framework.\n\n\n**Evaluating Angular\u0027s Impact**\n\nThe analysis shifts toward Angular\u0027s specific attributes. I\u0027m focusing on the significant implications of its use of TypeScript and its established CLI. I\u0027m considering how our proxying and routing strategies will integrate with the standard Angular project structure and build processes. The default port used by `ng serve` (4200) seems relevant to the integration plan.\n\n\n**Defining Angular Integration**\n\nI\u0027ve been examining the critical details of integrating Angular, leveraging my understanding of Angular\u0027s CLI, TypeScript, and standard project structures. I\u0027m finalizing the proposed changes to `gingee-cli add-app` to accommodate Angular. The configuration file `app.json` will be demonstrated next, highlighting port specifics and build output.\n\n\n**Adapting to Angular\u0027s Structure**\n\nNow I\u0027m focusing on the specifics of adapting the Gingee SPA architecture to accommodate Angular. I\u0027m deep into the `gingee-cli add-app` modifications, particularly its integration with the Angular CLI\u0027s folder structure, build processes, and typical project conventions. My attention now turns toward the precise alterations to `app.json` required for seamless Angular support.\n\n\n**Expanding to Angular\u0027s Structure**\n\nI\u0027m deep into the Angular integration phase, having established that the framework-agnostic backend handles this gracefully. Now I\u0027m detailing the `gingee-cli add-app` adjustments for Angular. My focus is on scaffolding the `src/` and necessary configuration files, mirroring standard Angular conventions. I\u0027m demonstrating the `app.json` adjustments, showcasing seamless proxying and build path configurations.\n\n\n",
