      "text": "**Initiating the Implementation**\n\nMy current focus is to move forward with the CLI enhancements, as the user has approved the engine changes. As per our roadmap, I\u0027m now setting up the implementation phase for these enhancements.\n\n\n**Confirming Implementation Details**\n\nI\u0027m now zeroing in on the specifics for the `add-app` command. My plan is to start with file-by-file changes, beginning with `gingee-cli/commands/addApp.js`. This will involve integrating `inquirer` to prompt for MPA/SPA selection. If SPA, it\u0027ll trigger the React + Vite + Tailwind CSS template generation. Key files to generate include `package.json`, `vite.config.js`, and `app.json`. I\u0027m structuring this as phase 1, step 3 (CLI Enhancements), making it easy to review.\n\n\n**Planning the Implementation**\n\nMy plan is to use a dedicated template directory with `fs-extra.copySync` for React + Vite + Tailwind CSS.  After the template is copied, I\u0027ll use `fs-extra.readJsonSync` and `writeJsonSync` to modify the template\u0027s `app.json`, inserting the appName and the JWT secret.  This makes the file generation much more streamlined and maintainable.\n\n\n**Finalizing Implementation Details**\n\nI\u0027m now integrating the proposed steps into the code. The plan is to create the template directory and use `fs-extra.copySync` for React + Vite + Tailwind CSS. Subsequently, `fs-extra.readJsonSync` and `writeJsonSync` will be used to customize the `app.json` file. The goal is to make the process efficient and easy to maintain.\n\n\n**Refining the Implementation Plan**\n\nNow, I\u0027m diving deeper into the technical aspects. My goal is to use a `templates/spa-react-vite` directory for generating the React + Vite + Tailwind CSS stack. I\u0027ll employ `fs-extra.copySync` to copy the template, and then modify the `app.json` file using `fs-extra.readJsonSync` and `writeJsonSync` to customize it with the app\u0027s name and JWT secret. This keeps my approach simple, clean, and easily maintainable.\n\n\n**Formulating Implementation Steps**\n\nI\u0027m now laying out the specific steps to generate a React + Vite + Tailwind CSS stack using a dedicated template directory. I\u0027ll employ `fs-extra.copySync` to handle the template copy, and modify the `app.json` file using `fs-extra.readJsonSync` and `writeJsonSync` to customize it with the app\u0027s name and JWT secret. This keeps my approach simple, clean, and easily maintainable. My next focus is on Gindoo.\n\n\n",
