      "text": "**Revisiting the Strategy**\n\nI\u0027ve been re-evaluating the approach based on the user\u0027s feedback. Modifying `gingee-cli` appears too complex, especially considering the diverse range of SPA frameworks. The original template was indeed too specific, as the user correctly pointed out. Now, I\u0027m exploring more generalized solutions, possibly involving a configurable system that allows for broader application.\n\n\n**Exploring Broader Solutions**\n\nI\u0027m now reconsidering the approach following the user\u0027s insightful concerns. The idea of modifying `gingee-cli` is becoming less appealing due to the inherent complexity it introduces. Maintaining bespoke CLI templates for every SPA framework combination is a daunting task, and I agree it goes against the \"lean and simple\" principle. Instead, I\u0027m now exploring broader solutions, possibly involving a more configurable system, to handle setup.\n\n\n**Seeking a Hybrid Path**\n\nI acknowledge the user\u0027s valid concerns about the maintainability of bespoke templates. I now realize building and maintaining templates for every potential combination of frameworks is unfeasible and runs contrary to the \"lean and simple\" philosophy of the project. I\u0027m exploring a hybrid solution that focuses on documentation, but also aims to smooth the onboarding process to reduce friction. This should make sure that the project is as easy to setup as possible, while also making sure that it is maintainable.\n\n\n**Crafting a Balanced Approach**\n\nI\u0027ve been meticulously analyzing the user\u0027s valuable critique. The core concern about template proliferation resonates deeply. Maintaining framework-specific templates is, indeed, impractical. I now lean toward a hybrid strategy that mitigates onboarding friction while avoiding the complexity of bespoke templates. My focus is on providing the necessary structure and configuration, leaving the frontend development to familiar tools and processes, and smoothing over the setup for new users.\n\n\n**Crafting a Refined Strategy**\n\nThe feedback was taken into account and I\u0027ve focused on maintaining the simplicity of `gingee-cli` while smoothing the onboarding for new users. The solution is to leverage `gingee-cli add-app`, allowing it to provide the essential Gingee scaffolding without becoming a framework expert. The idea is to create the base structure and a generic `app.json` while deferring the specific frontend setup to established tools. Then, I will provide clear instructions on next steps.\n\n\n**Smoothing Onboarding Friction**\n\nI\u0027m now implementing the hybrid solution. I\u0027ll leverage `gingee-cli add-app`, but the focus has shifted. Rather than framework-specific templates, it will generate a minimal Gingee scaffolding, a generic `app.json`, and clear instructions, minimizing the need for extensive CLI updates and making the workflow more accessible for new users. This approach addresses the user\u0027s concerns about long-term maintenance.\n\n\n",
