      "text": "Excellent. The framework-agnostic approach is a much more robust and sustainable strategy. We will proceed with this revised plan.\n\nThe implementation will now focus on making the Gingee core SPA-aware and providing the developer with the necessary backend structure and guidance, leaving them free to choose and configure their own frontend tooling.\n\nHere is the finalized implementation plan.\n\n---\n\n### **Final Implementation Plan**\n\n#### **Phase 1: Core Platform Enhancements**\n\nThis phase remains focused on updating the engine and tooling.\n\n**1. Update `gingee.js` (Engine Core)**\n\nThis is our first and most critical step. The server engine must be updated to handle SPA routing logic. The changes will be exactly as we discussed in the previous detailed plan:\n\n*   **Dependency:** Add `http-proxy-middleware` to the project.\n*   **`initializeApps` Function:** Update it to detect `type: \"SPA\"` in an `app.json` and, in development mode, automatically spawn the frontend\u0027s dev server as a child process.\n*   **`requestHandler` Function:** Update the routing logic to implement the \"API-first, then proxy/static/fallback\" routing priority for SPA-type apps.\n\n**2. Update `gingee-cli add-app` Command**\n\nThis is the core of our revised strategy. The command will now scaffold a minimal, framework-agnostic structure.\n\n*   **Action:** When a user runs `gingee-cli add-app my-app` and selects `SPA`, the CLI will:\n    1.  Create the directory `web/my-app/box/api`.\n    2.  Create a sample `web/my-app/box/api/hello.js`.\n    3.  Create the following commented `web/my-app/box/app.json`:\n\n    ```json\n    {\n      \"name\": \"my-app\",\n      \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n      \"type\": \"SPA\",\n      \"spa\": {\n        \"enabled\": true,\n        // IMPORTANT: Update this URL to match your frontend dev server\u0027s port.\n        // Vite\u0027s default is 5173, Angular\u0027s is 4200.\n        \"dev_server_proxy\": \"http://localhost:5173\",\n\n        // IMPORTANT: Update this path to match your build tool\u0027s output directory.\n        // Vite\u0027s default is \u0027../dist\u0027. Angular\u0027s is \u0027../dist/my-app/browser\u0027.\n        \"build_path\": \"../dist\",\n        \n        \"fallback_path\": \"index.html\"\n      },\n      \"db\": []\n    }\n    ```\n    4.  Print the following instructional message to the console:\n\n    ```\n    ✅ Success! Minimal SPA structure for \u0027my-app\u0027 created.\n\n    Your next steps are to set up your frontend project inside the new directory.\n\n    1. Navigate into your new app\u0027s folder:\n       cd web/my-app\n\n    2. Use your favorite tool to initialize your frontend project HERE.\n       For example, to use Vite + React, run:\n       npm create vite@latest . -- --template react\n\n    3. Install the frontend dependencies:\n       npm install\n\n    4. IMPORTANT: Review the generated \u0027box/app.json\u0027 and ensure the\n       \u0027dev_server_proxy\u0027 and \u0027build_path\u0027 match your frontend tooling.\n\n    5. Navigate back to the Gingee project root and start the server:\n       cd ../..\n       npm run dev\n    ```\n\n**3. Create New Documentation (`docs/spa-development-guide.md`)**\n\nTo support this new workflow, I will create a dedicated guide in the `docs/` folder. This guide will formalize the instructions provided by the CLI and give more detailed examples.\n\n*   **Title:** Gingee SPA Development Guide\n*   **Sections:**\n    *   **Core Concepts:** A brief explanation of Gingee\u0027s dev proxy and production fallback mechanism.\n    *   **Getting Started:** A step-by-step tutorial that follows the CLI output.\n    *   **Integration Recipes:**\n        *   A detailed section for \"Vite + React\".\n        *   A detailed section for \"Angular CLI\".\n        *   A detailed section for \"Vue + Vite\".\n        Each recipe will show the exact commands to run and any minor adjustments needed in `app.json`.\n    *   **Production Builds:** Best practices for configuring the `build_path` and `.gpkg` manifest for SPA deployment.\n\n---\n\nThis completes the plan for Phase 1. With these changes, the platform will be fully equipped to support modern SPA development in a flexible and maintainable way.\n\nI will now proceed with the implementation of these three tasks.",
