      "text": "**Revising the Architecture**\n\nI\u0027m currently focused on the user\u0027s request to migrate the Gindoo project\u0027s database from PostgreSQL to SQLite. The core architectural shift is clear, and I\u0027m assessing the impact. I\u0027ve pinpointed the key areas needing alteration, starting with the database abstraction layer to ensure compatibility. I\u0027m building a plan to seamlessly switch databases.\n\n\n**Updating Database Configurations**\n\nThe migration is moving forward with a focus on database configuration updates. My immediate concern is with `app.json` and the schema definitions. I\u0027m modifying the `db` settings to point to SQLite and adapting the SQL `CREATE TABLE` statements for SQLite\u0027s nuances. This involves changing data type definitions like `UUID` to `TEXT` and adjusting timestamps to SQLite-compatible `TEXT DEFAULT (datetime(\u0027now\u0027))` format. The goal is to maintain the database structure while ensuring compatibility.\n\n\n**Outlining Implementation Strategy**\n\nI\u0027m now formulating a detailed plan to handle this database switch. Key points are coming into focus: updating the `app.json` file to reflect the SQLite connection details and refining the `01_schema.js` file to ensure compatibility. The API scripts should remain intact because of the abstraction layer. I\u0027m shaping a structured response to convey these changes to the user.\n\n\n**Planning the Response**\n\nI\u0027m now building the user\u0027s response. I\u0027m structuring the plan by file: `app.json` and `01_schema.js`. I\u0027ll highlight the `db` configuration changes in `app.json` and the crucial data type modifications in `01_schema.js`. The key point is that existing API logic should remain unaffected, thanks to the database abstraction. I\u0027ll showcase this in the plan.\n\n\n**Refining the Implementation**\n\nI\u0027ve completed my analysis and outlined a detailed response for the user. My focus now is on presenting this in a way that is clear and easy to understand. I\u0027ll showcase the specific file modifications, like the updated `app.json` and the altered `01_schema.js`. Importantly, I\u0027m emphasizing that the existing API logic, because of the abstraction, remains unchanged. This will be the response.\n\n\n",
