      "text": "Understood. Switching to SQLite is an excellent choice for this application. It simplifies the setup by removing the need for an external database server and is a perfect demonstration of Gingee\u0027s multi-database capabilities.\n\nI will update the plan accordingly. The core API logic will remain the same, but the database configuration and the schema definition script need to be adjusted for SQLite\u0027s syntax and data types.\n\nHere is the revised backend implementation plan for Gindoo, now using SQLite.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Scaffolding (Unchanged)**\n\nThis step remains the same. We would run `gingee-cli add-app gindoo`, select `SPA`, and when prompted for a database, we would now select **`sqlite`**.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Update `app.json` for SQLite**\n\nThe CLI would generate this configuration based on our prompts. The key changes are the `type` and the `database` path, which now points to a file within the secure `box` folder.\n\n**File:** `web/gindoo/box/app.json`\n**Action:** Configure the `db` block for SQLite.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"Gindoo\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"type\": \"SPA\",\n  \"spa\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"dev_server_proxy\": \"http://localhost:5173\",\n    \"build_path\": \"../dist\",\n    \"fallback_path\": \"index.html\"\n  },\n  \"db\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"sqlite\",\n      \"name\": \"main_db\",\n      \"database\": \"data/gindoo.db\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"jwt_secret\": \"a_long_generated_secret_key_from_the_cli\",\n  \"startup_scripts\": [\n    \"setup/01_schema.js\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n*Notice how the connection details are now much simpler, pointing to a local file.*\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: Revise the Database Schema for SQLite Compatibility**\n\nSQLite uses different data types than PostgreSQL. I will update the startup script to use SQLite-compatible types. The common practice is to store UUIDs and Dates as `TEXT`.\n\n**Action:** Update the file `web/gindoo/box/setup/01_schema.js`.\n\n```javascript\n// File: web/gindoo/box/setup/01_schema.js\n\nmodule.exports \u003d async function() {\n    await gingee(async ($g) \u003d\u003e {\n        const db \u003d require(\u0027db\u0027);\n        const DB_NAME \u003d \u0027main_db\u0027;\n\n        $g.log.info(\u0027Running setup script for Gindoo with SQLite: 01_schema.js...\u0027);\n\n        // Create the Users table (SQLite compatible)\n        const createUsersTableSql \u003d `\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS \"Users\" (\n                \"id\" TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n                \"name\" TEXT NOT NULL,\n                \"email\" TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,\n                \"avatar_url\" TEXT,\n                \"created_at\" TEXT DEFAULT (datetime(\u0027now\u0027))\n            );\n        `;\n        await db.execute(DB_NAME, createUsersTableSql);\n        $g.log.info(\u0027Table \"Users\" is present.\u0027);\n\n        // Create the Tasks table (SQLite compatible)\n        const createTasksTableSql \u003d `\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS \"Tasks\" (\n                \"id\" TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n                \"title\" TEXT NOT NULL,\n                \"description\" TEXT,\n                \"status\" TEXT NOT NULL,\n                \"assignee_id\" TEXT REFERENCES \"Users\"(\"id\") ON DELETE SET NULL,\n                \"created_at\" TEXT DEFAULT (datetime(\u0027now\u0027)),\n                \"updated_at\" TEXT DEFAULT (datetime(\u0027now\u0027))\n            );\n        `;\n        await db.execute(DB_NAME, createTasksTableSql);\n        $g.log.info(\u0027Table \"Tasks\" is present.\u0027);\n\n        $g.log.info(\u0027Gindoo SQLite database schema setup is complete.\u0027);\n    });\n};\n```\n*The data types `UUID` and `TIMESTAMPTZ` have been changed to `TEXT`, and the default timestamp function is now SQLite\u0027s `datetime(\u0027now\u0027)`.*\n\n---\n\n### **Step 4: API Endpoints (Unchanged)**\n\nThis is a key advantage of Gingee\u0027s design. Because the `db` module provides a unified interface and the SQL we wrote is standard, our API scripts do not need to be modified. The `gingee-cli` uses the `pg` driver for PostgreSQL and the `better-sqlite3` driver for SQLite, but the developer-facing code in our scripts remains the same.\n\nThe `routes.json` and all the API scripts (like `api/tasks/list.js`) that I previously outlined are **fully compatible** with this new SQLite backend without any changes.\n\n---\n\nThe backend for Gindoo is now fully configured to use a simple, file-based SQLite database. The database file will be created automatically at `web/gindoo/box/data/gindoo.db` when the server first starts.\n\nWe are now ready to proceed with the frontend setup and implementation.",
