      "text": "**Considering Authentication Options**\n\nI\u0027m currently investigating what \"proper\" authentication entails for Gindoo, a modern SPA.  I\u0027m exploring several options, from basic username/password setups to more robust solutions like OAuth and JWT.  I\u0027m also considering the security implications of each approach.\n\n\n**Reviewing Authentication Flows**\n\nI\u0027m now diving into the user authentication flow. I\u0027ve considered several authentication methods and now I\u0027m evaluating the user login flow in detail.  Specifically, I\u0027m analyzing how to integrate a JWT-in-cookie approach. I\u0027m focusing on user registration, login, password verification, and cookie-based session management, aiming for security and simplicity. I\u0027m also ensuring the process complements Gingee\u0027s existing `auth` and `crypto` modules.\n\n\n**Implementing the Flow**\n\nI\u0027ve outlined a standard JWT-in-cookie authentication flow for Gindoo.  I\u0027ve defined the steps for user registration, login, and authenticated requests,  leveraging Gingee\u0027s `auth` and `crypto` modules.  The user registration flow will involve hashing passwords and storing user data.  Login entails password verification, JWT creation, and setting a secure, `HttpOnly` cookie. Middleware will then be utilized to protect API endpoints by validating the JWT and attaching user information to the request context.\n\n\n**Planning Implementation Details**\n\nNow I\u0027m focusing on the implementation strategy. I\u0027m breaking down the task into manageable steps: updating the database schema, creating the authentication API endpoints (register, login, logout, and me), developing the authentication middleware, and updating the configuration files. These steps will be done sequentially to ensure a smooth authentication system.\n\n\n**Refining Implementation Strategy**\n\nI\u0027m now refining the implementation plan for Gindoo\u0027s authentication system, concentrating on specific coding tasks.  I\u0027m addressing database schema modifications, including adding the password hash field.  I\u0027m also preparing for the API endpoint development, including registration, login, logout, and a \u0027me\u0027 route.  The goal is to create a secure, JWT-based authentication system. Specifically, I\u0027m working through how to generate and verify JWTs using `auth.jwt.create` and `auth.jwt.verify`.\n\n**Developing Implementation Plan**\n\nI\u0027m now deep-diving into the specific coding tasks and data structures required for the authentication system.  I\u0027m focusing on database schema modifications, API endpoint development (register, login, logout, me), and implementing the authentication middleware. I\u0027m also planning how to integrate JWT generation and validation using the Gingee `auth` module.\n\n\n**Outlining the Implementation Plan**\n\nI\u0027ve outlined a step-by-step implementation plan for Gindoo\u0027s authentication system. This involves database schema updates, API endpoint creation (login, register, logout, me), the implementation of an authentication middleware, and updating configuration files. The goal is a secure, JWT-based, standard cookie-based authentication solution. I\u0027m focusing on JWT generation and verification, cookie security, and middleware integration, with security a core consideration.\n\n\n",
