      "text": "Excellent. Let\u0027s begin the final implementation. We will proceed methodically, starting with the necessary backend changes to support the new authentication and permission model.\n\n---\n\n### **Phase 1: Backend API Enhancements**\n\n#### **Step 1: Simplify the Authentication Middleware**\n\nFirst, I will update the middleware. Its sole responsibility will now be to identify the user from their session cookie and attach their data (including their role) to the `$g` context object. This makes the user\u0027s information available to all subsequent API scripts without prematurely blocking requests.\n\n**Action:** Update the file `web/gindoo/box/auth_middleware.js`.\n\n```javascript\n// File: web/gindoo/box/auth_middleware.js\n\nmodule.exports \u003d async function() {\n    await gingee(async ($g) \u003d\u003e {\n        const auth \u003d require(\u0027auth\u0027);\n        const db \u003d require(\u0027db\u0027);\n        const DB_NAME \u003d \u0027main_db\u0027;\n\n        // Clear any previous user context to ensure a clean state for each request\n        $g.user \u003d null;\n\n        const token \u003d $g.request.cookies.gindoo_session;\n        if (token) {\n            const payload \u003d auth.jwt.verify(token);\n            if (payload \u0026\u0026 payload.userId) {\n                // If the token is valid, fetch the user\u0027s full details from the database\n                const user \u003d await db.query.one(\n                    DB_NAME, \n                    \u0027SELECT id, name, email, avatar_url, role FROM \"Users\" WHERE \"id\" \u003d $1\u0027, \n                    [payload.userId]\n                );\n\n                // If the user exists in the DB, attach them to the request context\n                if (user) {\n                    $g.user \u003d user;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    });\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n#### **Step 2: Create the \"Change Password\" API Endpoint**\n\nNext, I will create the new endpoint that allows a logged-in user to change their own password. It will use the `$g.user` object populated by the middleware to identify the user.\n\n**Action:** Create the file `web/gindoo/box/api/users/change-password.js`.\n\n```javascript\n// File: web/gindoo/box/api/users/change-password.js\n\nmodule.exports \u003d async function() {\n    await gingee(async ($g) \u003d\u003e {\n        const { db, crypto, utils } \u003d require(\u0027gingee\u0027);\n        const DB_NAME \u003d \u0027main_db\u0027;\n\n        // 1. Check if a user is logged in (populated by the middleware)\n        if (!$g.user) {\n            return $g.response.send({ error: \u0027Unauthorized. You must be logged in to change your password.\u0027 }, 401);\n        }\n\n        const { currentPassword, newPassword } \u003d $g.request.body;\n\n        // 2. Validate input\n        if (utils.validate.isEmpty(newPassword) || !utils.validate.hasLength(newPassword, { min: 8 })) {\n            return $g.response.send({ error: \u0027New password must be at least 8 characters long.\u0027 }, 400);\n        }\n\n        try {\n            // 3. Fetch the user\u0027s current password hash from the database\n            const userRecord \u003d await db.query.one(DB_NAME, \u0027SELECT password_hash FROM \"Users\" WHERE \"id\" \u003d $1\u0027, [$g.user.id]);\n            if (!userRecord) {\n                return $g.response.send({ error: \u0027User not found.\u0027 }, 404); // Should not happen if logged in\n            }\n\n            // 4. Verify the current password\n            const isPasswordCorrect \u003d await crypto.verifyPassword(currentPassword, userRecord.password_hash);\n            if (!isPasswordCorrect) {\n                return $g.response.send({ error: \u0027The current password you entered is incorrect.\u0027 }, 403);\n            }\n\n            // 5. Hash the new password and update the database\n            const newPasswordHash \u003d await crypto.hashPassword(newPassword);\n            await db.execute(DB_NAME, \u0027UPDATE \"Users\" SET \"password_hash\" \u003d $1 WHERE \"id\" \u003d $2\u0027, [newPasswordHash, $g.user.id]);\n\n            $g.response.send({ message: \u0027Password updated successfully.\u0027 });\n\n        } catch (err) {\n            $g.log.error(\u0027Failed to change password\u0027, { userId: $g.user.id, error: err.message });\n            $g.response.send({ error: \u0027An internal server error occurred.\u0027 }, 500);\n        }\n    });\n};\n```\n\nThis completes the first part of the backend updates. Please confirm to proceed with updating the task management endpoints and the route manifest.",
