      "text": "You are absolutely right. My apologies. This is a classic development scenario and a critical failure in my instructions.\n\nThe error `table Users has no column named role` is happening for a very specific reason:\n\n1.  When we first ran the application, the initial version of `01_schema.js` was executed, creating the `Users` table **without** the `role` column.\n2.  The command `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` does exactly what it says: since the `Users` table now exists, the script will not modify it on subsequent runs.\n3.  We then added the `02_seed_admin.js` script, which attempts to insert data into the `role` column.\n4.  Because the database file (`gindoo.db`) still contains the old table structure, the `INSERT` statement fails.\n\nThe solution is to reset your local database so that it can be recreated with the correct, updated schema.\n\nHere is the plan to fix this.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Stop the Server and Delete the Old Database**\n\nFirst, we need to stop the server to release any locks on the database file.\n\n**Action:**\n\n1.  Stop your Gingee server (press `Ctrl+C` in the terminal where `npm run dev` is running).\n2.  Delete the existing SQLite database file located at: **`web/gindoo/box/data/gindoo.db`**\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Ensure the Schema Script is Correct**\n\nLet\u0027s ensure your schema creation script is correct and includes the `role` column.\n\n**Action:** Verify that the file `web/gindoo/box/setup/01_schema.js` contains the following code.\n\n```javascript\n// File: web/gindoo/box/setup/01_schema.js\n\nmodule.exports \u003d async function() {\n    await gingee(async ($g) \u003d\u003e {\n        const db \u003d require(\u0027db\u0027);\n        const DB_NAME \u003d \u0027main_db\u0027;\n\n        $g.log.info(\u0027Running setup script for Gindoo with SQLite: 01_schema.js...\u0027);\n\n        // Create the Users table with the \u0027role\u0027 column\n        const createUsersTableSql \u003d `\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS \"Users\" (\n                \"id\" TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n                \"name\" TEXT NOT NULL,\n                \"email\" TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,\n                \"password_hash\" TEXT NOT NULL,\n                \"role\" TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT \u0027user\u0027, -- This line is crucial\n                \"avatar_url\" TEXT,\n                \"created_at\" TEXT DEFAULT (datetime(\u0027now\u0027))\n            );\n        `;\n        await db.execute(DB_NAME, createUsersTableSql);\n        $g.log.info(\u0027Table \"Users\" is present.\u0027);\n\n        // Create the Tasks table\n        const createTasksTableSql \u003d `\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS \"Tasks\" (\n                \"id\" TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n                \"title\" TEXT NOT NULL,\n                \"description\" TEXT,\n                \"status\" TEXT NOT NULL,\n                \"assignee_id\" TEXT REFERENCES \"Users\"(\"id\") ON DELETE SET NULL,\n                \"created_at\" TEXT DEFAULT (datetime(\u0027now\u0027)),\n                \"updated_at\" TEXT DEFAULT (datetime(\u0027now\u0027))\n            );\n        `;\n        await db.execute(DB_NAME, createTasksTableSql);\n        $g.log.info(\u0027Table \"Tasks\" is present.\u0027);\n\n        $g.log.info(\u0027Gindoo SQLite database schema setup is complete.\u0027);\n    });\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: Restart the Server**\n\nNow that the old database is gone and the schema script is correct, we can restart the server.\n\n**Action:**\n\n1.  Navigate to your Gingee project root.\n2.  Run the development server again:\n    ```bash\n    npm run dev\n    ```\n\n**What Will Happen Now:**\n1.  The Gingee server will start.\n2.  It will not find a `gindoo.db` file.\n3.  The `01_schema.js` startup script will run, and since the `Users` table does not exist, it will execute the `CREATE TABLE` command and create a **new** table with the correct schema, including the `role` column.\n4.  The `02_seed_admin.js` startup script will then run. This time, it will successfully insert the default admin user because the `role` column now exists.\n\nThe error will be resolved, and you will be able to log in with the default admin credentials. My apologies again for the oversight in the instructions.",
