      "text": "**Composing the App**\n\nI\u0027m currently working on the `App.tsx` file for Gindoo. It requires imports for React, `react-router-dom`, and all the essential page components like `LoginPage` and `KanbanPage`. This foundational structure will define the core navigation and rendering logic for our application. I\u0027ll meticulously ensure the correct components are imported to guarantee proper functionality.\n\n\n**Structuring the App.tsx**\n\nI\u0027ve been meticulously organizing the structure of `App.tsx` for Gindoo.  I\u0027ve incorporated imports for React, `react-router-dom`, and the page components like `LoginPage`, `KanbanPage`, `AdminUsersPage`, and context providers. Authentication guarding via `ProtectedRoute` is in place, alongside handling the initial session-checking loading state. The routing structure using `BrowserRouter` and `Routes` is set up, including the necessary `basename` for correct subpath operation. I\u0027m focusing on clearly defining public routes and routes protected by authentication.\n\n\n**Generating App.tsx**\n\nI\u0027m now fully immersed in the creation of the complete `App.tsx` file. I\u0027m meticulously incorporating all necessary imports, including `react-router-dom`, page components like `LoginPage`, `KanbanPage`, and context providers such as `AuthProvider` and `DataProvider`. My focus is on the `ProtectedRoute` component to handle authentication seamlessly. I\u0027ve designed the routing structure to handle the `/login` route publicly and secure the remaining routes with authentication, all within a `BrowserRouter` context with the correct `basename`.\n\n\n",
