      "text": "You are absolutely right. The screenshot clearly shows the layout breaking on smaller screens. My apologies for the faulty responsive classes in the `Navbar` component. The desktop menu is not being hidden, and the mobile menu is incorrectly positioned.\n\nThis is a classic Tailwind CSS responsiveness issue. I used `md:hidden` to hide the hamburger on medium screens and up, but I failed to correctly hide the **desktop** navigation on screens *smaller* than medium.\n\nI will now provide the definitive, corrected code for the `Navbar.tsx` component that properly implements a responsive hamburger menu.\n\n---\n\n### **Corrected `Navbar.tsx` for Full Responsiveness**\n\nThis updated code ensures that the desktop and mobile menus correctly toggle their visibility based on the screen size.\n\n**Action:** Please replace the entire contents of `web/gindoo/src/components/Navbar.tsx` with this final version.\n\n```tsx\n// File: web/gindoo/src/components/Navbar.tsx (Corrected)\n\nimport React, { useState } from \u0027react\u0027;\nimport { NavLink } from \u0027react-router-dom\u0027;\nimport { useAuth } from \u0027../contexts/AuthContext\u0027;\n\nexport const Navbar \u003d () \u003d\u003e {\n    const { user, logout } \u003d useAuth();\n    const [isMenuOpen, setIsMenuOpen] \u003d useState(false);\n\n    const getNavLinkStyle \u003d ({ isActive }: { isActive: boolean }) \u003d\u003e ({\n        borderBottom: isActive ? \u00272px solid #2563EB\u0027 : \u00272px solid transparent\u0027,\n        color: isActive ? \u0027#1F2937\u0027 : \u0027#6B7280\u0027,\n    });\n\n    // We define the set of links once to avoid repetition\n    const navLinks \u003d (\n        \u003c\u003e\n            \u003cNavLink to\u003d\"/\" end style\u003d{getNavLinkStyle} className\u003d\"hover:text-gray-900 py-2\"\u003e\n                Kanban\n            \u003c/NavLink\u003e\n            \u003cNavLink to\u003d\"/dashboard\" style\u003d{getNavLinkStyle} className\u003d\"hover:text-gray-900 py-2\"\u003e\n                Dashboard\n            \u003c/NavLink\u003e\n            {user?.role \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027admin\u0027 \u0026\u0026 (\n                \u003cNavLink to\u003d\"/admin/users\" style\u003d{getNavLinkStyle} className\u003d\"hover:text-gray-900 py-2\"\u003e\n                    Users\n                \u003c/NavLink\u003e\n            )}\n            {user?.role !\u003d\u003d \u0027admin\u0027 \u0026\u0026 (\n                \u003cNavLink to\u003d\"/profile\" style\u003d{getNavLinkStyle} className\u003d\"hover:text-gray-900 py-2\"\u003e\n                    Profile\n                \u003c/NavLink\u003e\n            )}\n        \u003c/\u003e\n    );\n\n    return (\n        \u003cheader className\u003d\"bg-white shadow-sm sticky top-0 z-40\"\u003e\n            \u003cdiv className\u003d\"container mx-auto px-6 py-3\"\u003e\n                \u003cdiv className\u003d\"flex justify-between items-center\"\u003e\n                    \u003ch1 className\u003d\"text-xl font-bold text-gray-800\"\u003eGindoo\u003c/h1\u003e\n                    \n                    {/* Desktop Menu: Hidden on screens smaller than md */}\n                    \u003cdiv className\u003d\"hidden md:flex items-center space-x-6\"\u003e\n                        \u003cnav className\u003d\"flex items-center space-x-8 text-sm font-medium\"\u003e\n                            {navLinks}\n                        \u003c/nav\u003e\n                        \u003cdiv className\u003d\"flex items-center\"\u003e\n                            \u003cspan className\u003d\"text-gray-600 text-sm mr-4\"\u003eWelcome, {user?.name}!\u003c/span\u003e\n                            \u003cbutton onClick\u003d{logout} className\u003d\"text-sm text-red-500 hover:text-red-700 font-medium\"\u003e\n                                Logout\n                            \u003c/button\u003e\n                        \u003c/div\u003e\n                    \u003c/div\u003e\n\n                    {/* Hamburger Button for Mobile: Visible only on screens smaller than md */}\n                    \u003cdiv className\u003d\"md:hidden\"\u003e\n                        \u003cbutton onClick\u003d{() \u003d\u003e setIsMenuOpen(!isMenuOpen)} className\u003d\"text-gray-600 hover:text-gray-800 focus:outline-none\"\u003e\n                            \u003csvg className\u003d\"w-6 h-6\" fill\u003d\"none\" stroke\u003d\"currentColor\" viewBox\u003d\"0 0 24 24\" xmlns\u003d\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"\u003e\n                                \u003cpath strokeLinecap\u003d\"round\" strokeLinejoin\u003d\"round\" strokeWidth\u003d\"2\" d\u003d\"M4 6h16M4 12h16m-7 6h7\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\n                            \u003c/svg\u003e\n                        \u003c/button\u003e\n                    \u003c/div\u003e\n                \u003c/div\u003e\n\n                {/* Mobile Menu Dropdown: Conditionally rendered */}\n                {isMenuOpen \u0026\u0026 (\n                    \u003cdiv className\u003d\"md:hidden mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-gray-200\"\u003e\n                        \u003cnav className\u003d\"flex flex-col space-y-4 text-sm font-medium\"\u003e\n                            {navLinks}\n                        \u003c/nav\u003e\n                        \u003cdiv className\u003d\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-gray-200\"\u003e\n                             \u003cspan className\u003d\"block text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"\u003eWelcome, {user?.name}!\u003c/span\u003e\n                             \u003cbutton onClick\u003d{logout} className\u003d\"w-full text-left text-sm text-red-500 hover:text-red-700 font-medium\"\u003e\n                                Logout\n                            \u003c/button\u003e\n                        \u003c/div\u003e\n                    \u003c/div\u003e\n                )}\n            \u003c/div\u003e\n        \u003c/header\u003e\n    );\n};\n```\n\n### **Summary of the Fix**\n\n1.  **Desktop Menu (`hidden md:flex`):** I have added the `hidden` class to the desktop `div`, which hides it by default. The `md:flex` class then makes it visible *only* on medium-sized screens and larger. This is the crucial part that was missing.\n2.  **Mobile Button (`md:hidden`):** The hamburger button is visible by default and then becomes hidden on medium screens and larger, which is the correct inverse of the desktop menu.\n3.  **Mobile Dropdown (`md:hidden`):** The dropdown menu containing the links is also correctly set to be hidden on medium screens and larger, ensuring it only appears on mobile.\n4.  **DRY Principle:** I have defined the set of `NavLink` components once and reused the `navLinks` variable in both the desktop and mobile sections. This makes the code cleaner and easier to maintain.\n\nThis corrected code will now function exactly as intended, displaying the full navigation on desktop and collapsing to a functional hamburger menu on mobile devices, resolving the layout issues shown in your screenshot.",
