      "text": "**Assessing the Issue**\n\nI\u0027m currently focused on the user\u0027s report regarding the missing scrollbar on the desktop version, which seemingly popped up after addressing responsive scrolling. My initial hunch, given the context, points toward a conflict in how we\u0027re handling height constraints or overflow properties, especially within the Kanban container. I\u0027m scrutinizing the recent changes in `Kanban` to pinpoint where this conflict might reside.\n\n\n**Refining the Hypothesis**\n\nI\u0027ve been meticulously examining the CSS logic, starting with `KanbanPage.tsx`. The fixed height established for the Kanban container seems sound on the surface. However, I\u0027m now focusing my attention on how `KanbanColumn.tsx` interacts with this fixed height. It\u0027s likely a miscalculation of available space within the flex container that\u0027s hindering the `overflow-y-auto` property from kicking in on the desktop. The interplay of `flex-grow` and `flex-shrink` within the columns is now under intense scrutiny.\n\n\n**Isolating the Conflict**\n\nI\u0027ve been re-evaluating the flow, tracing the height from `KanbanPage`\u0027s container down. I\u0027ve realized `KanbanColumn`\u0027s parent div *lacks* a definitive height set. This is preventing the `flex-grow` on the content div from working as intended, and thus, `overflow-y-auto` never activates. My focus has shifted toward setting an explicit height context within `KanbanColumn`.\n\n\n**Clarifying the Root Cause**\n\nI\u0027ve been examining the interplay of grid and flexbox properties, and realized the height inheritance is the key issue. Despite the fixed height of `KanbanPage`, `KanbanColumn` wasn\u0027t constrained. I\u0027ve now introduced `h-full` to the root `div` in `KanbanColumn` to ensure it respects the parent\u0027s boundaries, fixing the scroll issue.  This change aligns the column\u0027s height to the row within the grid, enabling `overflow-y-auto` to function correctly.\n\n\n**Revising the Fix**\n\nI\u0027ve been re-examining the fix and realized the previous solution was incomplete. While `h-full` on `KanbanColumn`\u0027s root addressed height inheritance issues and enabled scrollbars, it created another problem: the Kanban column\u0027s container grew past its parents bounds. I\u0027ve now introduced `h-full` to the root `div` in `KanbanColumn` *and* set its `overflow` to `hidden` to ensure it respects the parent\u0027s boundaries, fixing the overflow issue. This is now the proper fix!\n\n\n**Confirming the Resolution**\n\nI\u0027ve validated that the previous attempt did indeed have side effects. While setting `h-full` on `KanbanColumn`\u0027s root addressed the height inheritance and scrollbar issues, it created an overflow problem. My new fix introduces `overflow-hidden` to `KanbanColumn`, ensuring that it respects the parent\u0027s boundaries. This should prevent the container from growing beyond the grid row and correct the issue at hand.\n\n\n**Resolving the Scrollbar**\n\nI\u0027ve been examining the `KanbanColumn` component. I noticed that setting `h-full` to the root `div`, which fixes the scrollbar issue, created its own issues. It was expanding past the parent grid bounds. The `overflow-hidden` property will solve this.\n\n\n",
