      "text": "You are absolutely right. My apologies. I see the error in my implementation. In the process of adding the drag-and-drop functionality, I made the `TaskCard` component\u0027s main `div` a drag handle, which inadvertently disabled the `onClick` event meant for editing.\n\nThe `@dnd-kit` library\u0027s `listeners` prop takes over all pointer events (including clicks) for the element it\u0027s applied to. This is the direct cause of the bug.\n\nTo fix this, we need to separate the drag handle from the clickable area of the card. A common and effective pattern is to make only a specific \"drag\" icon or the title area the drag handle, leaving the rest of the card clickable. For simplicity and a large drag target, I will make the title the drag handle and the rest of the card\u0027s body the clickable \"edit\" area.\n\n---\n\n### **Corrected `TaskCard.tsx`**\n\n**Action:** Please replace the contents of `web/gindoo/src/components/TaskCard.tsx` with this corrected version.\n\n```tsx\n// File: web/gindoo/src/components/TaskCard.tsx (Corrected)\n\nimport React from \u0027react\u0027;\nimport type { Task } from \u0027../types\u0027;\nimport { useSortable } from \u0027@dnd-kit/sortable\u0027;\nimport { CSS } from \u0027@dnd-kit/utilities\u0027;\nimport { UserAvatar } from \u0027./UserAvatar\u0027;\n\ninterface TaskCardProps {\n    task: Task;\n    onClick: (task: Task) \u003d\u003e void;\n}\n\nexport const TaskCard \u003d ({ task, onClick }: TaskCardProps) \u003d\u003e {\n    const {\n        attributes,\n        listeners,\n        setNodeRef,\n        transform,\n        transition,\n        isDragging,\n    } \u003d useSortable({ id: task.id });\n    \n    const style \u003d {\n        transform: CSS.Transform.toString(transform),\n        transition,\n        opacity: isDragging ? 0.5 : 1,\n    };\n\n    return (\n        // The main div is now the droppable target, but not the drag handle.\n        \u003cdiv \n            ref\u003d{setNodeRef} \n            style\u003d{style} \n            className\u003d\"bg-white rounded-lg p-4 shadow-sm touch-none\"\n        \u003e\n            {/* 1. Header with Title (as Drag Handle) and Edit Button */}\n            \u003cdiv className\u003d\"flex justify-between items-start mb-2\"\u003e\n                \u003ch3 \n                    {...attributes} \n                    {...listeners} \n                    className\u003d\"font-medium text-gray-800 cursor-grab active:cursor-grabbing\"\n                \u003e\n                    {task.title}\n                \u003c/h3\u003e\n                \u003cbutton \n                    onClick\u003d{() \u003d\u003e onClick(task)} \n                    className\u003d\"text-xs text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 font-semibold\"\n                \u003e\n                    Edit\n                \u003c/button\u003e\n            \u003c/div\u003e\n\n            {/* 2. Body and Footer (Clickable for editing) */}\n            {/* We can wrap the rest of the content in a div with the onClick handler as well\n                to provide a larger clickable area. */}\n            \u003cdiv onClick\u003d{() \u003d\u003e onClick(task)} className\u003d\"cursor-pointer\"\u003e\n                {task.description \u0026\u0026 (\n                    \u003cp className\u003d\"text-sm text-gray-600\"\u003e\n                        {task.description}\n                    \u003c/p\u003e\n                )}\n                \u003cdiv className\u003d\"mt-4 flex justify-end items-center\"\u003e\n                    \u003cUserAvatar user\u003d{{ name: task.assigneeName, avatar_url: task.assigneeAvatar }} /\u003e\n                \u003c/div\u003e\n            \u003c/div\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n    );\n};\n```\n\n### **Summary of the Fix**\n\n1.  **Separated Concerns:** The drag-and-drop `listeners` and `attributes` are now applied only to the `\u003ch3\u003e` element containing the task title. This makes the title the specific \"drag handle\" for the card.\n2.  **Enabled `onClick`:** The `onClick` handler for editing is now applied to a separate \"Edit\" button and to the body of the card. Because these elements do not have the DnD `listeners` attached, their standard click events will now fire correctly.\n3.  **Improved UX:** I\u0027ve added a visible \"Edit\" button for better user affordance, so it\u0027s clear how to open the modal. The rest of the card body remains clickable for convenience. I also added `cursor-grab` to the drag handle to visually indicate that it\u0027s draggable.\n\nWith this change, users will be able to both drag tasks by their title and click on the \"Edit\" button (or the card body) to open the `TaskModal` as intended. This resolves the bug and restores the editing functionality.",
