        "text": "**Unpacking the Root Cause**\n\nI\u0027ve been meticulously analyzing the user\u0027s report. The core symptom, `$g.user` being `null` at the outset of `update.js`, is the key. It then miraculously becomes available later. This strongly suggests a timing issue, a race condition, or a problem with how the user data is initially loaded. I\u0027m focusing on the interaction between asynchronous operations and how the user object is populated.\n\n\n",
