      "text": "Excellent question. You are correct, while the backend API for deleting tasks is complete, I have not yet implemented the user interface for it.\n\nBased on our established rules, only an administrator should be able to delete tasks. Therefore, the \"Delete\" button should only be visible to a user with the `admin` role. The most logical place for this button is on the task card itself, allowing for quick removal of items from the board.\n\nHere is the plan and implementation to add this final piece of functionality.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Enhance `TaskCard.tsx` with Delete Functionality**\n\nI will modify the `TaskCard` component to include a delete button that is conditionally rendered. This component will get the user\u0027s role from the `AuthContext` and the `deleteTask` function from the `DataContext`.\n\n**Action:** Please replace the contents of `web/gindoo/src/components/TaskCard.tsx` with this complete and final version.\n\n```tsx\n// File: web/gindoo/src/components/TaskCard.tsx\n\nimport React from \u0027react\u0027;\nimport type { Task } from \u0027../types\u0027;\nimport { useSortable } from \u0027@dnd-kit/sortable\u0027;\nimport { CSS } from \u0027@dnd-kit/utilities\u0027;\nimport { useAuth } from \u0027../contexts/AuthContext\u0027;    // +++ IMPORT: To check user role\nimport { useData } from \u0027../contexts/DataContext\u0027;  // +++ IMPORT: To get the delete function\nimport { UserAvatar } from \u0027./UserAvatar\u0027;\n\ninterface TaskCardProps {\n    task: Task;\n    onClick: (task: Task) \u003d\u003e void;\n}\n\nexport const TaskCard \u003d ({ task, onClick }: TaskCardProps) \u003d\u003e {\n    const { user } \u003d useAuth();\n    const { deleteTask } \u003d useData();\n    const isAdmin \u003d user?.role \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027admin\u0027;\n\n    const {\n        attributes,\n        listeners,\n        setNodeRef,\n        transform,\n        transition,\n        isDragging,\n    } \u003d useSortable({ id: task.id });\n    \n    const style \u003d {\n        transform: CSS.Transform.toString(transform),\n        transition,\n        opacity: isDragging ? 0.5 : 1,\n    };\n\n    // +++ NEW: Handler for the delete button +++\n    const handleDelete \u003d async (e: React.MouseEvent) \u003d\u003e {\n        e.stopPropagation(); // Prevent the edit modal from opening\n        if (window.confirm(`Are you sure you want to delete the task \"${task.title}\"?`)) {\n            try {\n                await deleteTask(task.id);\n            } catch (err: any) {\n                alert(`Error: ${err.message}`); // Simple error feedback\n            }\n        }\n    };\n\n    return (\n        \u003cdiv \n            ref\u003d{setNodeRef} \n            style\u003d{style} \n            className\u003d\"bg-white rounded-lg p-4 shadow-sm touch-none border border-gray-200\"\n        \u003e\n            \u003cdiv className\u003d\"flex justify-between items-start mb-2\"\u003e\n                \u003ch3 \n                    {...attributes} \n                    {...listeners} \n                    className\u003d\"font-medium text-gray-800 cursor-grab active:cursor-grabbing pr-2\"\n                \u003e\n                    {task.title}\n                \u003c/h3\u003e\n                \u003cbutton \n                    onClick\u003d{() \u003d\u003e onClick(task)} \n                    className\u003d\"text-xs text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 font-semibold\"\n                \u003e\n                    Edit\n                \u003c/button\u003e\n            \u003c/div\u003e\n\n            \u003cdiv onClick\u003d{() \u003d\u003e onClick(task)} className\u003d\"cursor-pointer\"\u003e\n                {task.description \u0026\u0026 (\n                    \u003cp className\u003d\"text-sm text-gray-600 break-words\"\u003e\n                        {task.description}\n                    \u003c/p\u003e\n                )}\n                \u003cdiv className\u003d\"mt-4 flex justify-between items-center\"\u003e\n                    {/* +++ NEW: Conditionally rendered Delete Button for Admins +++ */}\n                    {isAdmin ? (\n                        \u003cbutton onClick\u003d{handleDelete} className\u003d\"text-xs text-red-500 hover:text-red-700 font-medium\"\u003e\n                            Delete\n                        \u003c/button\u003e\n                    ) : (\n                        \u003cdiv /\u003e // Empty div to keep the layout consistent for non-admins\n                    )}\n                    \u003cUserAvatar user\u003d{{ name: task.assigneeName, avatar_url: task.assigneeAvatar }} /\u003e\n                \u003c/div\u003e\n            \u003c/div\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n    );\n};\n```\n\n### **Summary of the Changes**\n\n1.  **Role Check:** The component now uses the `useAuth()` hook to get the logged-in user and determines if `isAdmin` is true.\n2.  **Delete Handler:** A new `handleDelete` function has been added. It stops the click from bubbling up (which would open the edit modal), shows a standard browser confirmation dialog, and then calls the `deleteTask` function from our `DataContext` if confirmed.\n3.  **Conditional Rendering:** The \"Delete\" button is now rendered inside the card\u0027s footer, but only if the `isAdmin` flag is true. This ensures that only administrators will see and be able to use the delete functionality.\n\nThis completes the final piece of core functionality for the Gindoo application. All user flows, including role-based permissions for deleting tasks, are now fully implemented.",
