      "text": "Thank you. I have received the updated `gingee.js` file and have thoroughly analyzed the changes.\n\nI understand the modification completely. This is an excellent and important architectural improvement.\n\n**My understanding of the key change is as follows:**\n\nThe `development` vs. `production` mode is no longer a global server setting determined by `process.env.NODE_ENV`. Instead, it has been moved to a per-application configuration. Each app can now have a `\"mode\": \"development\"` property in its `app.json` file.\n\nThis provides significantly more flexibility, allowing a developer to, for instance:\n*   Run a single SPA in development mode (with its Vite/Angular dev server and proxy active).\n*   While all other applications on the same Gingee instance continue to run in a stable, production mode, serving their built static assets.\n\nI have noted the specific implementation changes:\n1.  **In `initializeApps`:** A new default `\"mode\": \"production\"` is added to the `defaultAppConfig`, and the `isDevelopment` flag is now determined by the specific `appConfig.mode` for each application being loaded. This correctly controls when to spawn the SPA\u0027s development server.\n2.  **In `requestHandler`:** The `isDevelopment` flag is now derived from the currently matched `app.config.mode`, ensuring that the routing logic (proxy vs. static/fallback) is also handled on a per-app basis.\n\nMy internal context is now updated with this superior, more flexible engine logic. I am ready to proceed.",
