      "text": "Excellent point. Completing the project includes ensuring the documentation is up-to-date with our latest work. You are correct; our recent implementation of SPA support has introduced new concepts and configurations that are not reflected in the existing documentation.\n\nI have performed a comprehensive review of all the documentation files in the project. Several documents indeed require updates to be accurate and to properly guide developers using these new features.\n\nHere is a file-by-file breakdown of the necessary changes.\n\n---\n\n### **Documentation Update Analysis**\n\n**1. `docs/app-structure.md` (High Impact)**\n*   **Reason:** This is the primary reference for the `app.json` file. It\u0027s critically out of date.\n*   **Required Changes:**\n    *   Add a new top-level property section for `\"type\": \"SPA\"` to explain its function.\n    *   Add a new top-level property section for `\"mode\": \"development\" | \"production\"` to explain how it controls the app\u0027s runtime behavior (proxy vs. static serving).\n    *   Add a new major section detailing the `\"spa\"` configuration object and its properties (`enabled`, `dev_server_proxy`, `build_path`, `fallback_path`).\n\n**2. `docs/features.md` (High Impact)**\n*   **Reason:** We have implemented a major new platform feature.\n*   **Required Changes:**\n    *   Add a new feature bullet point under \"Key Platform Features\" titled **\"First-Class SPA Hosting \u0026 Development Workflow\"**.\n    *   The description should summarize the development proxy for a seamless, CORS-free experience and the production fallback routing for client-side routers.\n\n**3. `docs/gingee-cli.md` (High Impact)**\n*   **Reason:** The `add-app` command\u0027s behavior has fundamentally changed.\n*   **Required Changes:**\n    *   Update the `add-app` command\u0027s description.\n    *   Modify its \"Wizard Prompts\" list to include the new choice between `MPA` and `SPA`.\n    *   Add a clear description of the new, minimal backend structure that is scaffolded for the SPA option and the instructional guidance the CLI provides for setting up the frontend.\n\n**4. `docs/packaging-guide.md` (Medium Impact)**\n*   **Reason:** The packaging requirements for an SPA are different from an MPA.\n*   **Required Changes:**\n    *   In the section describing the `.gpkg` manifest, add a dedicated subsection or example for packaging an SPA.\n    *   This example must show the correct `include` patterns (including the `dist` folder) and `exclude` patterns (excluding `src`, `vite.config.js`, etc.) to create a clean production package.\n\n**5. `docs/concepts.md` (Medium Impact)**\n*   **Reason:** The high-level overview needs to be updated to reflect the new capabilities.\n*   **Required Changes:**\n    *   In the \"The Gingee Project Structure\" section, briefly mention that SPA projects will also contain frontend source folders like `src/` and a build output folder like `dist/`.\n    *   In the \"Flexible Routing Engine\" section, add a note about how SPA fallback routing complements the existing API routing.\n    *   In the \"Configuration\" section, briefly mention that `app.json` now includes a `type` and `mode` to support SPA hosting.\n\n**6. `docs/app-developer-guide.md` (Low Impact)**\n*   **Reason:** This guide is focused on the MPA/backend-first workflow. Trying to merge a full SPA tutorial would make it confusing.\n*   **Proposed Change:**\n    *   Add a prominent callout box near the beginning of the guide that says:\n        \u003e **Building a Single Page Application?**\n        \u003e This guide focuses on the classic Multi-Page App (MPA) workflow. For a complete tutorial on building modern SPAs with frameworks like React, Vue, or Angular, please see our dedicated **[Gingee SPA Developer\u0027s Guide](./spa-appdev-guide.md)**.\n\n**7. Documents That Do NOT Require Changes:**\n*   `docs/server-config.md`: The `gingee.json` file was not changed.\n*   `docs/server-script.md`: The `$g` object and the core script pattern remain the same.\n*   `docs/glade-admin.md`: Glade\u0027s functionality for installing/upgrading `.gin` packages works identically for SPAs and MPAs.\n*   `docs/permissions-guide.md`: The permissions model is unchanged.\n*   `docs/gstore-hosting-guide.md`: The process for hosting a store is independent of the app types.\n\n---\n\nThis plan ensures that our documentation is brought fully up-to-date with the platform\u0027s new capabilities. The changes will provide clarity for new developers and properly document the robust SPA features we have just built.\n\nShall I proceed with applying these updates to the documentation files?",
